      "rev_n_8_203757_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_203757_1",
        "node_id": "n_8_203757",
        "thought_text": "To accurately calculate the number of years it takes for Takahashi's balance to reach X yen or above, we need to use a more precise method that accounts for the compounding interest correctly. Instead of incrementing the balance by 1% each year, we should calculate the new balance using the formula for compound interest: \n\n\\[ \\text{new\\_balance} = \\text{current\\_balance} \\times (1 + \\text{interest\\_rate}) \\]\n\nThis approach ensures that the balance grows continuously according to the annual interest rate. We should also ensure that the loop exits as soon as the balance reaches or exceeds X yen, without running an unnecessary additional iteration.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "2520452287135048782",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_8_203757_0",
